4:   "summary": "Task: wad (WAD loading and sound/music integration), source digest 6ef3e2af.... Changed files: none. Inspection found no defect, so I made no edits.\n\nWhat I read: loop/acceptance.md, platform/README.md, build.sh, platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c, platform/doom_audio.c, web/audio.js, and the build-03 tester handoff. I did not open the other prior handoffs or process.json files. I did not run anything.\n\nFindings from reading the source:\n- WAD loading: build.sh preloads assets/doom1.wad to /doom1.wad. main() opens the file and checks for the \"IWAD\" magic. If the file is missing or invalid it shows a visible fatal message and returns, instead of failing silently. The engine is then started with -iwad /doom1.wad.\n- Sound: build.sh defines FEATURE_SOUND and builds platform/doom_audio.c. It also provides the SDL_mixer.h shim named in platform/README.md. Effects are read from the DMX lumps. They are validated (header, rate, length), converted to PCM and played through Web Audio with volume and pan.\n- Music: MUS scores are parsed. The parser rejects a bad header, truncated data, a missing end marker and an invalid delay. It plays through a small oscillator/noise synth.\n- Gesture gating: the AudioContext is created only in unlock(), which needs a user gesture. Until then effect() returns -1 and music is deferred.\n- Build: the build-03 tester's verify run passed at this same digest (build exit 0 in 3.98s, protected browser and audio tests exit 0 in 20.09s). That is prior evidence. I did not reproduce it.\n\nRemaining defects and limits (none are confirmed bugs):\n- Music is a simple synth, not OPL/GENMIDI, so musical fidelity is limited. GENMIDI is not used.\n- build.sh passes -w, which hides compiler warnings. It does not check the Emscripten version, so 4.0.18 is inferred from the successful build, not confirmed.\n- The 4s build time is unexplained. It may be cached.\n- The browser test cannot show actual audio output on speakers.\n- Not performed, and not established by this work: manual gameplay (doors, switches, focus transitions, saves, mouse aiming), autonomous repair, live resumption, and the teammate exercise (NOT PERFORMED, as the user requested). Historical cost is unknown.\n\nEvidence needed: a fresh tester verify run at the current digest, which should include the raw build log and the emcc --version output. There are no human-owned blockers.\n\nThis handoff is not acceptance.",
5:   "source_digest": "6ef3e2af1bf51ab5ffc051b67b311a2a3e889da805d322913d19fe02deb9af12"
6: }"}

