4:   "summary": "Scoped PASS for task \"wad\" (shareware WAD loading and sound/music integration) at source digest 6ef3e2af1bf51ab5ffc051b67b311a2a3e889da805d322913d19fe02deb9af12. This is a source review only. I executed nothing and ran no tests. Execution evidence is the build-03 tester's verify run at the same digest, which I did not reproduce.\n\nReviewed:\n- loop/acceptance.md\n- wad-01 coder handoff\n- build-03 tester handoff and its verification result.json and source.json\n- build.sh\n- platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c\n- platform/doom_audio.c\n- web/audio.js\n- tests/test_audio.py\n\nNot individually opened: the other prior handoffs and process.json files in the listed paths. I also did not open tests/browser.mjs or tests/test_browser.py. That the browser tests check nonzero effect and music samples is taken from loop/acceptance.md and the coder handoff.\n\nFindings:\n- WAD loading:\n  - build.sh:18 preloads assets/doom1.wad to /doom1.wad.\n  - platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c:128-135 checks for the \"IWAD\" magic. If the file is missing or invalid, it calls js_fatal, which sets the status text, logs console.error and sets Module.__fatal, and then returns 1. This is a visible failure, not a silent one.\n  - The engine is started with -iwad /doom1.wad (line 136).\n  - source.json records assets/doom1.wad in the digest, with sha256 1d7d43be....\n- Sound integration:\n  - build.sh:14 defines -DFEATURE_SOUND and compiles platform/doom_audio.c.\n  - platform/doom_audio.c defines DG_sound_module and DG_music_module. Effect lumps are resolved with the \"ds\" prefix and link handling, and the lump bytes are copied to JS.\n  - web/audio.js:76-101 validates the DMX header (bytes 0-1 equal 3,0), the rate range and the length against the lump size. It then converts the unsigned 8-bit samples, skipping the 16 pad samples at each end, and plays them with gain and pan. I found no out-of-bounds read.\n- Music:\n  - web/audio.js:5-33 parseMUS rejects a bad header, truncated data, a missing end marker, an unsupported event and an invalid delay.\n  - tests/test_audio.py asserts that all 13 bundled scores parse, that each rejects truncation by one byte, that a zeroed 16-byte header is rejected, and that no AudioContext exists after parsing.\n- Gesture gating: the AudioContext is created only in unlock() (audio.js:38). effect() returns -1 unless the context state is running (audio.js:77). Music registered before unlock gets its base time reset when the context is created (audio.js:52).\n- Execution evidence: artifacts/runs/loop-20261105T005309Z-73a58c79/build-03-739c40e3/tester/verification-c2ca2bd026bb/result.json says status PASS at this digest, with build exit 0 in 3.98s and the protected tests exit 0 in 20.09s. source.json shows the same digest.\n\nRegression risk: low. The coder made no edits for this task, and the source is identical to the digest the build-03 tester verified.\n\nUnresolved limits (none are confirmed defects):\n- No fresh tester run exists for the wad task itself. Only the build-03 run at the same digest backs this review.\n- build.sh:2 documents Emscripten 4.0.18 but does not enforce it. Nothing I read confirms the version actually used. The log and `emcc --version` output are not in the evidence.\n- build.sh passes -w, which hides compiler warnings.\n- The 4s build time is unexplained and may be cached or incremental.\n- Music uses a simple oscillator/noise synth, not OPL/GENMIDI, so musical fidelity is limited.\n- In doom_audio.c, Start() calls W_ReleaseLumpNum(lump) after the lump data has been copied with HEAPU8.slice, so the release is safe.\n\nNot established by this PASS (manual or uncovered):\n- door and switch activation\n- OS focus transitions\n- physical speaker output and musical fidelity\n- save persistence\n- mouse aiming\n- a manual playthrough\n\nFull capstone items are also not established: real autonomous repair, live resumption, accountability, design rationale and reflection. The teammate exercise is NOT PERFORMED, as the user requested. Historical token and cost usage is unknown. This PASS does not mean the full assignment is accepted.",
